   "text": "I read the structure as a lariat-type peptide of 18 residues. I traced it from the N-terminus, where a chloroacetyl-type CH2 closes a thioether ring onto the Cys side chain, to the C-terminal serinamide.\n\n**Sequence (N to C):**\nTyr \u2013 N-Me-Lys \u2013 Val \u2013 Val \u2013 Ser \u2013 Asn \u2013 Trp(5-OMe) \u2013 Phe(4-COOH) \u2013 Lys \u2013 Trp(5-OH) \u2013 Aib \u2013 Val \u2013 Cys \u2013 Gly \u2013 Pro \u2013 D-Ser \u2013 D-Ser \u2013 D-Ser-NH2\n\n- **Thioether:** the N-terminal acetyl CH2 is bonded to the sulfur of the Cys side chain, closing the macrocycle.\n- **N-Me-Lys side chain:** the \u03b5-NH is acylated by the \u03b3-carboxyl of a Glu. That Glu keeps its free \u03b1-COOH, and its \u03b1-NH is acylated by 4-(4-iodophenyl)butanoyl.\n- **Aib:** the quaternary carbon bearing two methyls is \u03b1-aminoisobutyric acid, so it has no stereocentre.\n- **Stereochemistry:** I assigned each \u03b1-carbon from its wedge or hash and the relative positions of its substituents. All residues come out L except the three C-terminal serines, which come out D. These assignments rest on my reading of the wedges and are the least certain part of the answer.\n\nSMILES: C1C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc(O)cc2)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](CCCCNC(=O)CC[C@@H](C(=O)O)NC(=O)CCCc2ccc(I)cc2)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](CO)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2c[nH]c3ccc(OC)cc23)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc(C(=O)O)cc2)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCN)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2c[nH]c3ccc(O)cc23)C(=O)NC(C)(C)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](CS1)C(=O)NCC(=O)N4CCC[C@H]4C(=O)N[C@H](CO)C(=O)N[C@H](CO)C(=O)N[C@H](CO)C(N)=O"
